"Release notes  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog)\nciteturn993view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog\",\"lineno\":50}); Total lines: 967\nL0: [Button: ]\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search]\nL3: \nL4: `/`\nL5: \nL6:   * English\nL7:   * Deutsch\nL8:   * Español – América Latina\nL9:   * Français\nL10:   * Indonesia\nL11:   * Italiano\nL12:   * Polski\nL13:   * Português – Brasil\nL14:   * Shqip\nL15:   * Tiếng Việt\nL16:   * Türkçe\nL17:   * Русский\nL18:   * עברית\nL19:   * العربيّة\nL20:   * فارسی\nL21:   * हिंदी\nL22:   * বাংলা\nL23:   * ภาษาไทย\nL24:   * 中文 – 简体\nL25:   * 中文 – 繁體\nL26:   * 日本語\nL27:   * 한국어\nL28: cite0†Get API key†aistudio.google.com cite1†Cookbook†github.com cite2†Community†discuss.ai.google.dev Sign in\nL29: \nL30: cite3†Docs cite4†API reference L31: \nL32: [Input: Filter]\nL33: \nL34: [Button: ]\nL35: \nL36:   * Get started\nL37: \nL38:   * Models\nL39:   * Lyria 3.5 & Lyria Clip\nL40: \nL41:   * Robotics\nL42: \nL43:   * Core capabilities\nL44: \nL45:   * Image\nL46: \nL47:   * Video\nL48: \nL49:   * Speech and audio\nL50: \nL51:   * Thinking\nL52: \nL53:   * Agents\nL54: \nL55:   * Tools\nL56: \nL57:   * Live API\nL58: \nL59:   * Get started\nL60: \nL61:   * cite5†Thinking L62:   * Optimization\nL63: \nL64:   * Guides\nL65: \nL66:   * File input\nL67: \nL68:   * Logs and datasets\nL69: \nL70:   * Safety\nL71: \nL72:   * Frameworks\nL73: \nL74:   * Resources\nL75: \nL76:   * Migration\nL77: \nL78:   * cite6†Status†aistudio.google.com L79:   * Google AI Studio\nL80: \nL81:   * Google Cloud Platform\nL82: \nL83:   * Policies\nL84: \nL85: [Button: Send feedback ]\nL86: # Release notes\nL87: \nL88: This page documents updates to the Gemini API.\nL89: ## September 17, 2026\nL90: \nL91:   * Antigravity Agent 09-2026: Released `antigravity-preview-09-2026`, which replaces and deprecates `antigravity-preview-05-2026`.\nL92: \nL93: If you run on a remote sandbox (`environment: \"remote\"`) and read only `output_text` or `model_output` steps, update the agent string and nothing else changes.\nL94: If you run tools locally (`local_environment`) or parse `function_call` steps, the built-in tools changed. Parameters use PascalCase instead of snake_case, and file edits use line-range replacements instead of full rewrites.\nL95: Capability  | 05-2026  | 09-2026\nL96: --- | --- | ---\nL97: File creation  | `write_file(path, content)`  | `write_to_file(TargetFile, CodeContent, Overwrite, Description)`\nL98: File editing  | `write_file(path, content)`, full rewrite  | `replace_file_content(TargetFile, StartLine, EndLine, TargetContent, ReplacementContent)`\nL99: File reading  | `read_file(path, offset, limit)`, byte offsets  | `view_file(AbsolutePath, StartLine, EndLine, ContentOffset)`\nL100: Directory listing  | `list_files(path)`  | `list_dir(DirectoryPath)`\nL101: File and code search  | None, agents used shell commands  | `find_by_name(SearchDirectory, Pattern, MaxDepth)` and `grep_search(SearchPath, Query, IsRegex)`\nL102: Shell execution  | `code_execution(command, timeout_seconds)`  | Unchanged\nL103: Web search  | `google_search(queries)`  | Unchanged\nL104: See the cite7†Antigravity Agent guide. `antigravity-preview-05-2026` shuts down on October 5, 2026, tracked on the cite8†deprecations page.\nL105: ## September 15, 2026\nL106: \nL107:   * Gemini 3.8 Live and Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking generally available (GA): Released two new audio-to-audio models for real-time voice applications using the Live API:\nL108:     * Gemini 3.8 Live (cite9†`gemini-3.8-live` ): The default option for most low-latency voice agent experiences and real-time dialogue without reasoning delays. Features interleaved reasoning, default asynchronous function calling, and full session client content updates.\nL109:     * Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking (cite10†`gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking` ): High-reasoning audio-to-audio model supporting background reasoning during live audio interactions, recommended when higher background reasoning is required.\nL110: To get started, see the cite11†Live API guide , the cite12†Capabilities guide , and the cite5†Thinking guide .\nL111: ## September 3, 2026\nL112: \nL113:   * Lyria 3.5 generally available (GA): Released the next generation of Google's music generation model:\nL114: \nL115:     * cite13†`lyria-3.5` : Full-length song generation with improved musical coherence, natural vocals, and fine-grained duration and structural control.\nL116: \nL117: The model supports text and image inputs and generates high-fidelity 44.1 kHz stereo audio. See the cite14†Music generation guide for details and code samples.\nL118: ## September 2, 2026\nL119: \nL120:   * Gemini 3.8 Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-3.8-flash`, our most intelligent Flash model, engineered for long-horizon software engineering, autonomous agents, and complex enterprise workflows.\nL121: \nL122: To get started, see the cite15†Gemini 3.8 Flash model page and the cite16†Latest model guide .\nL123: ## September 1, 2026\nL124: \nL125:   * Agentic video understanding: Released agentic video understanding for Gemini 3.7 Flash, 3.6 Flash, and 3.5 Flash-Lite across the Interactions and GenerateContent APIs. The model dynamically navigates video timelines, requesting transcripts, frames, or audio tracks on demand. This approach uses up to 88% fewer tokens for long-form content compared to static processing.\nL126: \nL127: To get started, see the cite17†Agentic video understanding guide.\nL128: ## August 27, 2026\nL129: \nL130:   * Gemini Omni Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-omni-1.1-flash`, the GA version of our fast, conversational video generation and editing model. This release includes significant new capabilities:\nL131:     * Video extension: Seamlessly extend existing videos by generating continuations at the end of a clip using the `extend` task or directly with a prompt.\nL132:     * Interpolation (first + last frame): Generate a video transitioning between two images using the `image_to_video` task with up to 2 images.\nL133:     * Resolution control: New `resolution` parameter in `video_config` supports `360p`, `720p` (default), `1080p`, and `4k` outputs. 1080p and 4K outputs are generated using upscaling.\nL134: The existing `gemini-omni-flash-preview` endpoint will be deprecated on September 30, 2026.\nL135: \nL136: To get started, see the cite18†Gemini Omni Flash model page and the cite19†omni guide .\nL137: ## August 26, 2026\nL138: \nL139:   * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe generally available (GA): Released two dedicated speech-to-text models based on Gemini's audio understanding:\nL140:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe (`gemini-3.5-transcribe`): High-accuracy, low-latency non-streaming speech-to-text with utterance-based language detection across 85+ languages, speaker diarization, word-level timestamps, and custom vocabulary biasing (up to 1,000 terms).\nL141:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe Live (`gemini-3.5-transcribe-live`): Low-latency, bidirectional streaming speech-to-text over WebSockets using the Live API, supporting interim and finalized transcription events, Smart transcription mode, and multiple Voice Activity Detection (VAD) strategies.\nL142: To get started, see the cite20†Audio transcription guide , the cite21†Live transcription guide , and the cite22†Gemini 3.5 Transcribe model page .\nL143: ## August 13, 2026\nL144: \nL145:   * Gemini 3.7 Flash generally available (GA): Released our most intelligent workhorse model yet for coding and agents:\nL146: \nL147:     * Gemini 3.7 Flash (`gemini-3.7-flash`): Substantial improvements across software engineering, web development, and agentic workflows, available at an introductory price through December 31, 2026.\nL148: \nL149: To get started, see the cite23†Gemini 3.7 Flash model page and the cite16†Latest model guide .\nL150: ## July 30, 2026\nL151: \nL152:   * Gemini Robotics ER 2 in public preview: Released two new embodied reasoning model endpoints for robotics:\nL153: \nL154:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-preview`: Advanced spatial reasoning, agentic code execution, multi-step tool orchestration, video moment finding, progress classification, and multi-robot coordination.\nL155:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-streaming-preview`: Optimized for real-time text streaming using the Live API, enabling low-latency robot agents with bidirectional audio and video input.\nL156: Both model endpoints accept text, image, video, and audio inputs and support function calling with blocking behavior for physical robot actions. To get started, see the cite24†Gemini Robotics ER overview . For real-time streaming use cases, see cite25†Robotics with streaming .\nL157: \nL158:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` model will be cite26†shut down on August 31, 2026.\nL159: ## July 21, 2026\nL160: \nL161:   * Gemini 3.6 Flash and Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite generally available (GA): Released stable, production-ready versions of our latest 3.x Flash models:\nL162:     * Gemini 3.6 Flash (`gemini-3.6-flash`): Features improved token efficiency and code/agentic planning capabilities at a lower price point than 3.5 Flash, resolving developer feedback around output verbosity.\nL163:     * Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite (`gemini-3.5-flash-lite`): Offers a low-latency, highly cost-effective subagent option designed for high-volume automation.\nL164: \nL165: To learn more, see the cite16†Latest Gemini model guide.\nL166:   * Deprecated parameters: The sampling parameters `temperature`, `top_p` and `top_k` are now deprecated. See the cite27†Latest Gemini Model for details.\nL167: ## July 6, 2026\nL168: \nL169:   * cite28†Developer logs support for the Interactions API: logs for supported Interactions API calls are now viewable in the cite29†AI Studio dashboard†aistudio.google.com .\nL170: ## June 30, 2026\nL171: \nL172:   * Gemini Omni Flash in public preview: Released `gemini-omni-flash-preview`, a high-performance multimodal model designed for high-speed video generation and conversational video editing. Using the cite30†Interactions API , you can generate 3–10 second videos at 720p from text descriptions or animate still images, and then conversationally edit and refine the outputs. To get started, see the cite19†Gemini Omni Flash guide and the cite18†Gemini Omni Flash model card.\nL173:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` (Nano Banana 2 Lite) to general availability (GA), our built-in multimodal model optimized for ultra-low latency and cost-effective image generation and editing. See the cite31†Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Image model card and the cite32†Image generation guide.\nL174: ## June 24, 2026\nL175: \nL176:   * Computer Use: Launched public preview support for the cite33†Computer Use tool in Gemini 3.5 Flash. This release includes simplified actions with intents, built-in support for browser, mobile, and desktop environments, configurable safety policies, and advanced prompt injection detection.\nL177: ## June 17, 2026\nL178: \nL179:   * Streaming support for speech generation: Streaming via `streamGenerateContent` (and `stream: true` in the Interactions API) is now supported for the `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview` model. To learn more, see the cite34†Text-to-Speech guide.\nL180: ## June 15, 2026\nL181: \nL182:   * Deprecation announcement: The following image generation models are being deprecated and will be cite26†shut down on August 17, 2026:\nL183: \nL184:     * Imagen 4 and Gemini 3 Image models:\nL185:       * `imagen-4.0-generate-001`\nL186:       * `imagen-4.0-ultra-generate-001`\nL187:       * `imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001`\nL188: \nL189: To migrate your code to newer stable or preview endpoints, refer to the cite35†Gemini deprecations page.\nL190:   * Deprecation announcement: The following video generation models are being deprecated and will be cite26†shut down on June 30, 2026:\nL191: \nL192:     * Veo models:\nL193:       * `veo-2.0-generate-001`\nL194:       * `veo-3.0-generate-001`\nL195:       * `veo-3.0-fast-generate-001`\nL196: Update your integration to either use the Veo 3.1 preview model IDs (`veo-3.1-generate-preview`, `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`) or the 3.1 GA models available through the cite36†Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform†docs.cloud.google.com to avoid service interruptions.\nL197: \nL198:   * Deprecation announcement: The experimental GMP Contextual View tool (a fixed interface for Grounding with Google Maps outputs) will cite26†shut down on June 15, 2026:\nL199: ## June 1, 2026\nL200: \nL201:   * The following Gemini 2.0 models are now cite26†shut down :\nL202: \nL203:     * `gemini-2.0-flash`\nL204:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-001`\nL205:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite`\nL206:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001`\nL207: \nL208: Use cite37†`gemini-3.5-flash` or cite38†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL209: ## May 28, 2026\nL210: \nL211:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-image` (Nano Banana 2) and `gemini-3-pro-image` (Nano Banana Pro), the generally available (GA) versions of our native visual models, cite39†Gemini 3.1 Flash Image and cite40†Gemini 3 Pro Image .\nL212:   * Video-to-image generation support: You can now pass a video file (via direct upload or as a public YouTube URL) as multimodal context alongside a text prompt to generate high-quality thumbnails, cinematic movie posters, or summary infographics. This feature is supported exclusively on the `gemini-3.1-flash-image` model. To learn more, see the cite41†Video-to-image generation guide.\nL213:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` models are deprecated and will be cite26†shut down on June 25, 2026.\nL214: ## May 25, 2026\nL215: \nL216:   * The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model has been cite26†shut down . Use cite38†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL217: ## May 19, 2026\nL218: \nL219:   * Released `gemini-3.5-flash`, the generally available (GA) version of cite37†Gemini 3.5 Flash , our most intelligent model for sustained frontier performance on agentic and coding tasks. This is now the model behind `gemini-flash-latest`.\nL220:   * Launched the Managed Agents in the Gemini API in public preview. This enables developers to build and deploy autonomous, stateful agents that run in secure, isolated Google-hosted Linux sandbox environments. To learn more, see the cite42†Agents overview page and the cite43†Quickstart .\nL221:   * Released the general-purpose Antigravity Agent managed agent, cite44†`antigravity-preview-05-2026` , in public preview. The Antigravity agent can autonomously plan, reason, write and execute code, manage files, and browse the web inside its sandbox container. See the cite7†Antigravity Agent guide for code samples and specifications.\nL222: ## May 7, 2026\nL223: \nL224:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, the generally available (GA) version of cite38†Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite , optimized for speed, scale, and cost efficiency.\nL225: \nL226:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model is deprecating on 5/11/26 and will be cite26†shut down on May 25, 2026.\nL227: ## May 6, 2026\nL228: \nL229:   * Upcoming breaking change: The cite30†Interactions API request and response schema (`outputs` → `steps`) and output format configuration (`response_format`) are changing. The new schema becomes the default on May 26 and the legacy schema will be removed on June 8. See the cite45†migration guide for details.\nL230: ## May 5, 2026\nL231: \nL232:   * Updated File Search to support multimodal search. You can now natively embed and search through images using the `gemini-embedding-2` model. Grounding metadata now includes `media_id` for visual citations and `page_numbers` that indicate where information is found. To learn more, see the cite46†File Search guide.\nL233: \nL234: ## May 4, 2026\nL235: \nL236:   * Launched event-driven cite47†Webhooks support in the Gemini API to replace polling workflows for the Batch API and long-running operations.\nL237: ## April 30, 2026\nL238: \nL239:   * The `gemini-robotics-er-1.5-preview` model has been cite26†shut down . Use cite48†`gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` instead.\nL240: \nL241: ## April 22, 2026\nL242: \nL243:   * Released `gemini-embedding-2` as generally available (GA). To learn more, see the cite49†Embeddings page.\nL244: ## April 21, 2026\nL245: \nL246:   * Released new versions of the cite50†Deep Research agent with collaborative planning, visualization support, MCP server integration, and File Search:\nL247: \nL248:     * cite51†`deep-research-preview-04-2026` : Designed for speed and efficiency, ideal to be streamed back to a client UI.\nL249:     * cite52†`deep-research-max-preview-04-2026` : Maximum comprehensiveness for automated context gathering and synthesis.\nL250: ## April 15, 2026\nL251: \nL252:   * Launched cite53†Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS Preview , our cost-efficient, expressive, and steerable text to speech model. Read the cite54†Text-to-Speech docs to learn more.\nL253: ## April 14, 2026\nL254: \nL255:   * Released `gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview`, our updated robotics model. It now has new capabilities like instrument reading, improved spatial and physical reasoning capabilities. To learn more, see cite24†Gemini Robotics ER page and the cite55†blog†deepmind.google .\nL256: \nL257:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-robotics-er-1.5-preview` model will be cite26†shut down on April 30, 2026 at 9AM PST.\nL258: ## April 2, 2026\nL259: \nL260:   * Released `gemma-4-26b-a4b-it` and `gemma-4-31b-it`, available on cite56†AI Studio†aistudio.google.com and through the Gemini API, as part of the cite57†Gemma 4 launch.\nL261: \nL262: ## April 1, 2026\nL263: \nL264:   * Introduced the new cite58†Flex and cite59†Priority inference tiers, offering more options for optimizing cost or latency.\nL265: ## March 31, 2026\nL266: \nL267:   * Launched Veo 3.1 Lite Preview, cite60†`veo-3.1-lite-generate-preview` , our most cost-efficient cite61†video generation model, designed for rapid iteration and building high-volume applications.\nL268: \nL269:   * The `gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025` model has been shut down. Use cite62†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` instead.\nL270: ## March 26, 2026\nL271: \nL272:   * Released cite63†`gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview` , the latest audio-to-audio (A2A) model designed for real-time dialogue and voice-first AI applications. Read the cite11†Live API docs to get started.\nL273: ## March 25, 2026\nL274: \nL275:   * Launched cite14†Lyria 3 music generation models: cite64†`lyria-3-clip-preview` (30-second clips) and cite65†`lyria-3-pro-preview` (full-length songs). Both models accept text and image inputs and generate high-quality, 48kHz stereo audio. See the cite14†Music generation guide for details and code samples.\nL276: \nL277: ## March 23, 2026\nL278: \nL279:   * Rolled out cite66†Prepay and Postpay billing plans in AI Studio. Existing accounts may be affected; read the cite66†Billing documentation for more information.\nL280: ## March 18, 2026\nL281: \nL282:   * Released the new cite67†Built-in Tools and Function Calling Combination feature, making it possible to use Gemini's built-in tools alongside custom function calling tools in a single API call.\nL283:   * cite68†Grounding with Google Maps is now supported for Gemini 3 models going forward.\nL284: \nL285: ## March 16, 2026\nL286: \nL287:   * Introduced revamped cite69†Usage Tiers and cite70†Billing Account spend caps for a better user billing experience.\nL288: ## March 12, 2026\nL289: \nL290:   * Introduced cite71†project-level spend caps to billing in AI Studio.\nL291: \nL292: ## March 10, 2026\nL293: \nL294:   * Released `gemini-embedding-2-preview`, our first multimodal embedding model. It supports text, image, video, audio, and PDF inputs, mapping all modalities into a unified embedding space. To learn more, see cite49†Embeddings .\nL295: \nL296:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025` model will be cite26†shut down on March 31, 2026.\nL297: ## March 9, 2026\nL298: \nL299:   * The Gemini 3 Pro Preview model has been cite26†shut down . The `gemini-3-pro-preview` now points to cite72†`gemini-3.1-pro-preview` .\nL300: \nL301: ## March 3, 2026\nL302: \nL303:   * Launched Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite Preview, the first Flash-Lite model in the Gemini 3 series. Read the cite62†model page for specs, specific updates, and developer guidance.\nL304: ## February 26, 2026\nL305: \nL306:   * Launched Nano Banana 2, cite73†Gemini 3.1 Flash Image Preview , a high-efficiency model optimized for speed and high-volume use cases.\nL307: \n"